APC/NtMapViewOfSection/SetWindowsHookEx | [I] `nm -D --undefined-only f`; python `pefile` imports; MITRE T1055.x map | med-high (cheap enum/boolean fields: `has_injection` false, `injection_apis` []) |\n134\t| 79 | Embedded dynamic-trace template + env-gated branches | gap (present in every member D2-D18, unasked) | `\"schema\":\"huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1\"`, `\"branch\":\"`, `\"event_count\":`, `\"family\":\"<lang>_<theme>_trace\"`, `\"effects\":\"...\"`, `\"network\":\"none\"`; env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` with `analysis`/`sandbox`/`workstation` | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep -E 'dynamic_trace\\|family\\|HUNTRESS_'`; static branch map from the case table; sandboxed run with the env set (bwrap, no network) only if static fails | med-high (a backfill asking family/effects/branch per group is cheap for organizers) |\n135\t| 80 | Anti-analysis gating (sandbox/analysis/decoy branches, VM/debugger checks) | gap (D18 had `event_sandbox`/`event_decoy` + host-model gate) | env/host-model compare, `TracerPid`, `ptrace(TRACEME)`, CPUID hypervisor bit, VM vendor strings, timing via rdtsc/clock_gettime | [I] capstone/rizin xrefs to the compare strings; static only | med (natural sequel to the D18 sandbox/decoy branches) |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"457eaf39-a8b1-4d3e-9a0d-f840150d9475","uuid":"ca903aad-1418-4eba-8b09-6c2262cbb269","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:18:36.685Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md","content":"# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D20 post-run, 2026-10-20)\n\nScope: what a D21+ `evidence.zip` group (or backfilled old-group id) could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\nare. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D20), `challenges/day20/binary-resourceful/solver/`,\n`lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`, `wasm_layout`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n\nProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\nlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix (`stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`);\nD17 Ada ELF + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids: old days' single-solve facts re-asked on their groups + the `hcfg_storage` enum after a\nmid-day contract revision); D18 Fortran ELF (theme \"call graph / no injection\" unasked, CORRECT T+11 s). **D19 \"Jack in the Box\"\n(static-unpacking)** = ONE GnuCOBOL ELF (11 KB, `libcob.so.1`, stripped) whose HCFG is NOT in the image: a `PK19` overlay is\nappended after the section-header table (`PK19|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le len|sha256[32]|packed`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`, sha256-check,\nHCFG at out[0]). FIRST day whose prompt theme WAS asked on its own group: config_* only after unpacking + NEW `overlay_offset`\n(offset of the last magic) / `overlay_size` (file length - offset). The question text spelled the whole stub; 228 ids = 216 + 12,\nno backfill; CORRECT T+2:25, TT 4 s / Mastery (5 sets) 10 s first try; overlay 10808/424 constant across variants.\n**D20 \"Resourceful\" (resources-and-overlays)** = ONE Haskell ELF (GHC 9.12.2, 1.2 MB, dynamic libgmp, not stripped) + a 463-B\n`RS20` overlay at e_shoff+e_shnum*64: `RS20|ver@4|u32le res_len@8|u16le scratch_len@12|sha256(scratch)@16|HCFG resource@48 (RAW)|\nscratch` (\"private-scratch:<campaign>:inert-only\"). 240 ids = 228 + 12; NEW `hcfg_resource_size` (= u32le @8, 380). The prebuilt\nRS20/question-spec unpacker + raw HCFG scan banked 239 ids at T+27 s; one field branch -> CORRECT T+49 s, 0 wrong; TT 4.8 s /\nMastery 9.3 s first try; overlay constant across variants. D19-D20 = a \"hidden storage\" arc (packed overlay -> resource overlay;\nprompt: \"resources, overlays, bytes past the end of the sections ... map every boundary\").\n**Forward hints still open**: `neko_bytecode` in the format enum (unseen through D20); d07 `method_count` text: \"for Day 26 use the\nprimary classfile named by that unit\" (=> a JVM classfile member on D26 whose primary class is named by the question, not the\nmanifest). No new magic token in the D20 contract (no `XX21`): D21's twist is unannounced.\nLessons for D21+: (a) read the longest question of each new family first -- it is the layout spec; (b) every `*_size`/`*_offset`/\n`*_sha256` id maps to ONE named header field: parse the spec into a struct and expose every field; (c) grep each contract for\ntokens/days that are not today's; (d) header ids of the new member are answered by the carried-over solver; the twist is the new\nfield family; (e) `none` only for ABSENT things; (f) unguessable labels get fixed by contract revision -- re-pull.\nAsked field names: config_*, format (enum), machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols,\nsection_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol,\nhas_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset,\nhcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods, overlay_offset, overlay_size,\nhcfg_resource_size.\nRemaining risks: (1) D21 continues the storage arc with an unannounced container spot (section slack/caves, ELF notes,\ncompressed sections, multi-entry resource tables, appended archives, PE .rsrc/certificate) -- the question will spell the layout;\n(2) a backfill asking RS20/PK19 header facts (scratch_size, scratch_sha256, overlay_version, k1/k2, packed_length) or\n`hcfg_storage` for overlay-stored blobs; (3) Neko bytecode labels (architecture/machine for a VM); (4) D26 JVM classfile member;\n(5) per-language fact backfills (D8-D20 groups).\n\nTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\nInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\nllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\nrizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\nAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\njadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\nlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).\nMissing: qemu-user(-static), wasm-ld/lld, wasmtime, capa, Detect-It-Easy (diec), de4dot, monodis, erlang (beam_disasm),\nunluac/luajit-decompiler (luac present), blutter, srecord (srec_cat), binutils-multiarch, checksec, python zstandard/brotli, rzpipe/r2pipe.\n\n## Concept table\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D20+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | C ELF (gcc, glibc) | seen D1, D15 (+ every day's d01; D17 re-asked marker/recover_code) | `GCC: (...)` in `.comment`, `.interp` ld-linux, `__libc_start_main` | [I] `readelf -hSW f; readelf -sW f; objdump -d -M intel f` | high (carry-over every day; mastery d01 re-rolls stripped/renamed) |\n| 2 | C++ Itanium ELF / MinGW PE32+ | seen D2 | `_Z` symbols, `_ZTV`/`_ZTI`/`_ZTS`, `libstdc++`; PE `.text$_Z...` COMDAT, `.CRT`, `.tls` | [I] `nm -C f`; `objdump -t f.exe`; `c++filt` | high (carry-over; ELF/PE re-rolls per member) |\n| 3 | .NET C# PE (pe_cli) | seen D3 | `BSJB` metadata root `v4.0.30319`, `mscoree.dll`/`_CorExeMain`, `.runtimeconfig.json` | [I] `ilspycmd f.dll`; python `dnfile` | high (carry-over) |\n| 4 | Go (static, stripped; PE in Mastery) | seen D4 | `\\xff Go buildinf:`, `.gopclntab`, `runtime.`, `go1.NN` | [I] `GoReSym -t -d -p f`; `go version -m f`; `lib.binary.go_buildinfo` | high (carry-over) |\n| 5 | Rust ELF (debug_info) | seen D5 | `_ZN...17h<16hex>E` / `_R` v0 symbols, `rustc version`, `/rustc/<sha>/library` panic paths | [I] `rustfilt < syms`; `readelf -p .comment f` | high (carry-over) |\n| 6 | Rust stripped / release | gap | no `.symtab`, panic strings + `/rustc/<40hex>/` paths remain, `core::fmt` strings | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep -m3 /rustc/`; Ghidra headless; [M] no cargo-rustc symbol-recovery tool | med (natural \"stripped\" sequel for any language) |\n| 7 | Java / Kotlin jar | seen D6, D7 (D17 re-asked methods/access_flags/method_count/has_coroutine_runtime) | `PK` + `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF`, `CAFEBABE` classes, `kotlin/` packages | [I] `unzip -l f.jar; javap -v -p -c Main.class`; `jadx -d out f.jar`; `lib.binary.jar_app_classes` | high (carry-over) |\n| 8 | Swift ELF (static stdlib, 67 MB) | seen D8 | `swift5_*` sections, `$s` symbols, `libswiftCore` | [I] `bin/swift-demangle`; regex `SENGR` in `.rodata` | high (carry-over) |\n| 9 | Nim / D / Crystal ELF | seen D9, D11, D13 | Nim `NimMain`,`fatal.nim`; D `_D4core`,`DMDH`; Crystal `Crystal:H`,`GC_malloc` | [I] `bin/nim-demangle`; `grep -abo 'SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/=]*' f` | high (carry-over) |\n| 10 | Zig ELF + PE | seen D10 | `.comment` \"zig-bootstrap\"/LLD 19, stripped, `.hcfg` section | [I] `readelf -p .comment f; readelf -x .hcfg f` | high (carry-over) |\n| 11 | Free Pascal ELF | seen D12 | `FPC 3.2.2`, `.fpcdata`, `FPC_` symbols, static stripped | [I] `strings -a f \\| grep FPC`; `grep -abo HCFG f` | high (carry-over) |\n| 12 | Objective-C (GNUs