n  {\"id\": \"theme-facts-recording\", \"concept\": \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's (overlay_offset/overlay_size, config after unpacking) and D20's (overlay_offset, hcfg_resource_size) WERE and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NO\n  {\"id\": \"fortran-gfortran-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"gfortran facts for the d18 group when its theme is backfilled: source file name, MAIN__, internal procedures (name.N), select_string case table, libgfortran imports, .comment GCC banner\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixtures: copy the cached d18 members (single variant-000 + TT/Mastery variants under challenges/day18/binary-flow-state/solver/cases/*/artifacts) into tests/data/binary_fixtures (gfortran compiler is NOT installed; runtime libgfortran.so.5 is). Facts: source_file `variant-000.f90` (S\n  {\"id\": \"callgraph-indirect-flow-facts\", \"concept\": \"Generic call graph with indirect-call resolution for ELF/PE: per-function callees, PLT import edges, `mov/lea reg, imm; call reg` targets, call-table/jump-table targets, entry->main chain\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D18 prompt: 'Reconstruct the call graph ... follow the calls' (unasked). Implement lib.binary.call_graph(data) with capstone linear sweep over FUNC symbols (fallback: .eh_frame FDE ranges / rizin `aaa;aflj` when stripped): direct `call rel32` -> callee symbol or PLT import name (r\n  {\"id\": \"api-intent-injection-classifier\", \"concept\": \"Classify each imported/called API by intent and give an injection verdict (ELF 