g case arrays, Go/Rust match tables\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 dispatched on `_gfortran_select_string` + cmp chain; a stripped or -O2 sequel uses a real jump table. Implement lib.binary.switch_tables(data): find `jmp reg` preceded by a bounded index (cmp/ja) and a table base (lea rip+x), read N entries, map case -> target address -> symbol. Fix\n  {\"id\": \"anti-analysis-gating-facts\", \"concept\": \"Anti-analysis / sandbox gating facts: environment and host-model checks, decoy branches, debugger/VM detection (TracerPid, ptrace TRACEME, CPUID hypervisor bit, DMI/VM vendor strings, rdtsc timing)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 had event_sandbox/event_decoy branches selected by HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL -- an 'evasion' theme is a natural next day. Facts: anti_debug (bool + technique list: ptrace_traceme, tracerpid, isdebuggerpresent, ntqueryinformationprocess, timing), anti_vm (cpuid_hypervisor, vm_strings list), env_gates [e\n  {\"id\": \"flattened-dispatcher-recovery\", \"concept\": \"Control-flow flattening (OLLVM-style state-variable dispatcher) and opaque predicates: recover the original block order / state transitions\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Title pun 'Flow State' -> state machine; OLLVM is not installed, so hand-write fixtures: C with `switch(state)` inside `while(1)` where each case sets the next state (constants xor'd), plus opaque predicates `x*(x+1)%2==0`. Extractor: identify the dispatcher (block with most predecessors + cmp/jmp on one stack var), emulate each case with unicorn to read\n  {\"id\": \"gcc-frontend-modula2-member\", \"concept\": \"Next GCC front-end languages as a new-day member: Modula-2 (gm2), COBOL (gcobol, GCC 15), Algol 68 (ga68), gccgo\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"NOT BUILT (1st attempt failed). D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL: the organizers walk a 'legacy/GCC-family language' list, each landing as a plain dynamic ELF. Remaining: Modula-2 (gm2: NEEDED libm2pim/libm2iso/libm2rts, `_M2_<Module>_init`/`_fini`), gccgo (libgo.so.23, `__go_`, `.go_export`, NO `.go.buildinfo`), Algol 68 (ga68), gcobol (GCC 15 COBOL: `libgcobol.so`, `__gg__` -- d\n  {\"id\": \"multi-layer-overlay-chain\", \"concept\": \"Nested / decoy overlays: several magic hits, earlier decoy overlay with a bad hash, payload that is itself an ELF or another overlay\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Find the FINAL PK19 overlay' implies the generator knows multiple overlays. Fixtures: (a) two PK19 blocks, first with a wrong sha256 (decoy), (b) a magic string inside .rodata (code that checks it) before the real overlay, (c) unpacked payload = a tiny ELF whose own overlay/HCFG holds the config, (d) overlay inside the overlay. Rule set: prefer the LAST magic whos\n  {\"id\": \"decoder-stub-emulation\", \"concept\": \"Find the unpacking stub in code and emulate it over the overlay when the question does NOT spell the transform (timed mutations)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 prompt: 'Find the stub, watch it work ... statically'. The question spelled ror8(b^k2,3)^k1, but a mutated variant may only say 'unpack the overlay'. Locate: code that reads the file (/proc/self/exe open + lseek(end)/fseek) or references the magic constant (cmp dword, 0x39314b50 = 'PK19' LE), then a byte loop with xor/ror/rol/add/sub immediates; extract the op sequenc\n  {\"id\": \"cobol-gnucobol-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"GnuCOBOL facts for the d19 group when its theme/identity is backfilled: libcob version, program-id, source file, NEEDED list, cob_* imports, COBOL runtime boolean\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 member (cached: challenges/day19/binary-jack-in-the-box/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d19--variant-000.elf): stripped dynamic ELF, NEEDED libcob.so.1, libm.so.6, libvbisam.so.1, libgmp.so.10, libncurses.so.5, libtinfo.so.5, libdl.so.2, libc.so.6; imports cob_init, cob_save_call_params, cob_call_params, cob_check_version, cob\n  {\"id\": \"haxe-vm-targets\", \"concept\": \"Haxe family beyond Neko: HashLink bytecode (`HLB`), hxcpp native ELF, nekotools-booted executables\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If Neko lands, the same Haxe source may come as other targets (a pair day: `-neko`/`-hl`, or 'one source, two VMs'). With haxe installed (apt haxe 4.3.7): `haxe -main Main -hl out.hl` (HashLink magic `HLB` + version u8; strings table holds the HCFG), `-neko out.n`, and `nekotools boot out.n` (ELF neko VM + bytecode appended; the bytecode overlay begins with `NEKO`, boot trailer `NEKO` + u32 offset at the end\n  {\"id\": \"packer-decompressors\", \"concept\": \"Decompressors used by real packers for overlay payloads: aPLib, LZNT1, LZMA raw/LZMA86, LZ4 block, LZSS/LZ77 custom, RLE/PackBits\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A 'static unpacking' sequel (RS20 or Mastery mutations) may compress before the byte transform. Implement pure-Python aPLib (depack), LZNT1, LZSS (4096 ring, 0x20 fill), PackBits/RLE and LZ4 block (python lz4 installed) in lib.binary with try-order by magic/entropy; lzma.FORMAT_RAW with lc3/lp0/pb2 dict 64 KB for raw LZMA. Fixtures: compress an HCFG with each (aPLib via a \n  {\"id\": \"elf-notes-custom-storage\", \"concept\": \"HCFG stored in a custom ELF note (SHT_NOTE `.note.<vendor>` / PT_NOTE): namesz/descsz/type parsing with 4/8 alignment\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture: gcc ELF with `objcopy --add-section .note.huntress=note.bin --set-section-flags .note.huntress=alloc,readonly` (+ a PT_NOTE variant via linker script). Parser: pyelftools iter_notes + raw fallback walking (namesz, descsz, type) with alignment. Expose note owners/types JSON in table order, the desc offset of the HCFG (offset convention: the `H`), has_<owner>_note.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"compressed-elf-sections\", \"concept\": \"SHF_COMPRESSED sections (Elf64_Chdr ch_type 1 zlib / 2 zstd) and legacy `.zdebug_*` (`ZLIB` + u64be size) holding the HCFG\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: `objcopy --add-section .hcfg=blob --compress-debug-sections` does not touch non-debug sections, so write Chdr + zlib manually (ch_type, ch_size, ch_addralign) and set SHF_COMPRESSED (0x800); also a `.zdebug_hcfg` legacy one. Decoder: python zlib; zstd needs `pip install zstandard` into .venv (missing) or the `zstd` CLI. Expose compressed size, uncompressed size (ch_s\n  {\"id\": \"haskell-ghc-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"GHC + RS20 facts for the d20 group when its theme/identity is backfilled: GHC version, hsLibs/UnitLinkOpts, Main_main closures, has_ghc_runtime, rts options; RS20 header fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: copy the cached d20 members (single variant-000 + TT/Mastery variants under challenges/day20/binary-resourceful/*/). Facts: ghc_version from the `9.12.2`-style string near `ProjectVersion`/hsLibs (`-lHSghc-internal-9.1202.0`), base version 4.21.0.0, NEEDED [libm, libgmp, libc], `.debug-ghc-link-info` present, gold-\n  {\"id\": \"pe-certificate-overlay\", \"concept\": \"PE overlay coexisting with an Authenticode certificate table (Security directory points into the file tail), PE checksum, overlay start vs cert range\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If the storage arc moves to PE (d02/d04/d10 already re-roll PE in Mastery): overlay start = max(PointerToRawData+SizeOfRawData); DIRECTORY_ENTRY_SECURITY VirtualAddress is a FILE offset; HCFG may sit after the WIN_CERTIFICATE (dwLength, wRevision 0x0200, wCertificateType 2) or inside its padding. Fixtures: MinGW PE (x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc if present, \n  {\"id\": \"js-runtime-single-executable\", \"concept\": \"Node SEA / Deno compile / Bun --compile / pkg single executables: locate the embedded JS + resources by note/section/trailer\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node SEA: ELF note/section `NODE_SEA_BLOB` (postject) + fuse string `NODE_SEA_FUSE_fce680ab2cc467b6e072b8b5df1996b2:1`; Deno: trailer `d3n0l4nd` + u64 offsets at EOF; Bun: `\\\\n---- Bun! ----\\\\n` trailer with module graph; pkg: `PAYLOAD_POSITION`/`PRELUDE_POSITION` placeholders. Fixtures can be synthetic (small ELF + trailer layout) since real ones are ~100 MB. Expose em\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-language-family-classfile\", \"concept\": \"D26 JVM classfile member (leaked: 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'): Scala/Clojure/Groovy jars or a standalone .class; pick the class the question names\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend the d07 method_count path: accept a classfile name from the question text ('primary classfile named by that unit') instead of the manifest Main-Class; handle a bare `CAFEBABE` member (format label? jar enum token does not fit -> watch the enum), Scala (`ScalaSignature`/`ScalaSig` attribute, `$` companion class\n  {\"id\": \"de4dot\", \"concept\": \"ConfuserEx / .NET string encryption\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github de4dot-cex (ViRb3) release; needs apt mono-runtime. `de4dot F -o clean.dll` then ilspycmd.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"erlang-lua-decompilers\", \"concept\": \"BEAM, Lua, LuaJIT bytecode\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"luac (lua5.4) is now installed. Still missing: apt erlang-base (beam_lib/beam_disasm), unluac jar (sourceforge), luajit-decompiler-v2 (github marsinator358) -- only if a bytecode container appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"binutils-multiarch\", \"concept\": \"objdump/readelf for MIPS/PPC/SPARC/RISC-V\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install binutils-multiarch; rizin, llvm-objdump-18 and Ghidra already cover disassembly, so this is a convenience only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ihex-srec-firmware\", \"concept\": \"Intel HEX / S-record / raw firmware members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"objcopy -I ihex|srec -O binary already converts (srecord not needed). For raw blobs: rizin -a arm -b 16 -m <base>; format label unknown (`ihex`/`srec`/`raw`?) -> submit alone.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dart-aot-snapshot\", \"concept\": \"Dart AOT executable (`dart compile exe`): snapshot sections, HCFG inside the isolate snapshot (possibly compressed/obfuscated)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `_kDartVmSnapshotData`, `_kDartIsolateSnapshotData/Instructions` symbols, `Dart_` runtime strings, ELF appended to dartaotruntime (or a standalone ELF in recent SDKs). Strings in the snapshot are stored as OneByteString objects (raw latin-1 with header) -> raw scan works unless compressed pointers/obfuscation; fallback search for SENGR base64. Record snapshot hash (32 hex)\n  {\"id\": \"backfill-language-identity-facts\", \"concept\": \"Per-language identity + theme facts for the D8-D17 groups (the next backfill): has_<lang>_runtime / has_<lang>_mangled_symbol / class, protocol, selector, proc, template names\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 re-asked D1-D7's single-solve facts on their old groups (marker, recover_code, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-classfile-facts\", \"concept\": \"Full JVM ClassFile facts for jar groups (d06/d07): versions, constant-pool count, this/super/interfaces, fields, methods+descriptors, attributes, Kotlin metadata\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 asked methods (names, table order, incl <init>), access_flags (decimal 49) and method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>) of the Main-Class. Next backfill may ask major_version/minor_version, constant_pool_count, ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-metadata-facts\", \"concept\": \".NET metadata facts for the d03 group: assembly name/version, MVID, TypeDef/MethodDef names, FieldRVA, TargetFramework, entry point token\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). d03 is the only old group whose day-facts were not re-asked on D17 (it got hcfg_version/xor_key_hex only); a later backfill likely asks typedef/method names, method_count, assembly_name, assembly_version, ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"decoder-routine-locator\", \"concept\": \"Locate and characterise the config DECODER in the binary: function name, algorithm (xor/add/rol/rc4...), key/immediate, loop length, references to the stored blob\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 prompt: 'Recover the reversible decoder' (unasked, but a later backfill may ask decoder facts on d17 or any HCFG group). From the validated HcfgHit: compute blob VA, find code xrefs (RIP-relative lea/mov to VA in ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"native-imports-exports-facts\", \"concept\": \"imports / NEEDED / interpreter / exports lists for ELF, PE, Mach-O\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Generic facts: ELF `needed` (DT_NEEDED order), `imports` (UND .dynsym names, table order, version suffix stripped), `interpreter` (.interp without NUL), `exports` (defined dynsyms); PE import dll list + functions ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"provenance-facts-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Build provenance fields: GNU build-id, .comment compiler banner, DWARF producer/language/comp_dir, PE TimeDateStamp/PDB path/Rich, Go/Rust toolchain version\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Implement in the facts dict so a new id answers without code: build_id = lowercase hex of NT_GNU_BUILD_ID desc (no 0x), compiler = first `.comment` string, dwarf_producer via pyelftools, pdb_path from RSDS, timestamp as ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"language-detector\", \"concept\": \"lib.binary.language_of(data) -> source language/toolchain token with evidence, for all 17 seen languages + next candidates\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). A `language`/`compiler`/`toolchain` id on any group would need consistent tokens: c, cpp, csharp/dotnet, go, rust, java, kotlin, swift, nim, zig, d, pascal/fpc, crystal, objc, wat/wasm, ada; candidates haskell, ocaml, ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"emulate-return-value\", \"concept\": \"Recover a function's return value by emulation when it is not a `mov eax, imm; ret` leaf (obfuscated/computed/OLLVM recover_code)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). recover_code was re-asked D17; a mutated variant may compute the constant (xor of two imms, lookup table, flattened switch). unicorn x86-64 (installed): map the ELF PT_LOADs, set rsp to a scratch stack, run from the ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"api-hashing-resolver\", \"concept\": \"Imports resolved by hash (ROR13, djb2, FNV-1a, CRC32, murmur) -> resolved API list / hash algorithm fields\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Natural 'encoded' sequel to D17 for a decoder-themed day. Precompute hash tables for libc/kernel32/ntdll export names under the common algorithms; scan .rodata/.text immediates (capstone `cmp`/`mov` imm32) and report ...\"},\n  {\"id\": \"per-string-encryption\", \"concept\": \"Every string (not just HCFG) encrypted individually with a shared decoder (xor/add per string, stack strings) -> decoded string lists as fields\", \"priority\": 3, \"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/457eaf39-a8b1-4d3e-9a0d-f840150d9475/tool-results/bv7pt69k4.txt","persistedOutputSize":40386},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016hm2StT5pa9HdidHwSHBQH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
