{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LKQ4kELEe1Nb9v7QwPtt4S","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-21; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n5\t  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n6\t- One `evidence.zip` (AES, password `infected`). From Day 3 on it is CUMULATIVE: members `dNN--variant-XXX.<ext>`, one group per\n7\t  past day, plus ONE new container/language per day: D1 C ELF, D2 C++ (ELF or MinGW PE32+), D3 .NET dll, D4 static stripped Go,\n8\t  D5 static Rust, D6 Java .jar, D7 Kotlin fat .jar, D8 Swift ELF (67 MB), D9 Nim, D10 Zig (PE `.exe` in Mastery), D11 D (DMD),\n9\t  D12 Free Pascal, D13 Crystal, D14 Objective-C (GNUstep), D15 a PAIR of C ELFs (`-stripped`/`-symbolized`), D16 a PAIR of WASM\n10\t  modules (`-compact`/`-direct`), D17 Ada ELF (GNAT 14.2), D18 Fortran ELF (gfortran), D19 GnuCOBOL ELF + packed `PK19`\n11\t  overlay, **D20 Haskell GHC 9.12.2 ELF** (1.2 MB, dynamic libgmp/libm/libc, not stripped, `.debug-ghc-link-info` section)\n12\t  **with an `RS20` resource overlay** (plain HCFG resource + private \"scratch\" bytes + sha256), **D21 a LOADER/PLUGIN pair**\n13\t  (`-loader.elf` OCaml 4.02.3 native PIE + Dynlink, `-plugin.cmxs` OCaml natdynlink shared object; HCFG RAW in the plugin's\n14\t  `.data`). Since D18 the new day is a binary-STRUCTURE theme: call graph (D18), packing (D19), resources/overlays (D20), shared\n15\t  libraries / loader handshake (D21: \"Trace the exports, the imports, and the loader's handshake, and mind the boundaries\").\n16\t  Answer ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`; a multi-member group adds a member qualifier:\n17\t  `dNN_analysis_<qualifier>_<field>` (D15 `stripped_`/`symbolized_`, D16 `compact_`/`direct_`, D21 `loader_`/`plugin_`). D21 also\n18\t  has UNQUALIFIED ids on a 2-member group whose QUESTION names the member (\"Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member; the loader has no\n19\t  scored HCFG config\") -- route by the question text, not only by the id.\n20\t- From Day 2 on, every new-day member carries the same embedded **HCFG** config blob: `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16 len (LE) |\n21\t  u32 crc32 | xor'd JSON` (JSON at offset 12; crc32 is over the decoded plaintext). Only its storage changes (`.hcfg` section\n22\t  D2/D10/D14, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata, base64 in a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim/D/Crystal literal, RAW in FPC\n23\t  `.data`, WASM data segment 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`) -- D19: NOT byte-visible (unpacked payload of the appended PK19\n24\t  overlay); D20: RAW again, at +48 inside the appended RS20 overlay (a plain `HCFG` scan finds it). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND its base64 form `SENGR...` (crc-gate every hit); when both miss, look\n25\t  for an overlay past the ELF image and read the question text -- it spells the unpacker.\n26\t  The JSON carries never-asked keys too (ipv4, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model): parse the whole dict.\n27\t- The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for `exact_text` fields\n28\t  (format, machine, symbol, D17 `hcfg_storage`). **The organizers RE-ISSUE the contract mid-day** when a label is unguessable\n29\t  (D17 `hcfg_storage` -> `kind: enum` + ordered rule list). Since D17 the question texts are SPECS: D19's config questions give\n30\t  the whole unpacking algorithm byte by byte. `format` is now `kind: enum` on d12-d19: `elf, pe, pe_cli, jar, wasm, neko_bytecode`.\n31\t- **The contract LEAKS future days**: D19's `format` enum listed `neko_bytecode` (still unseen on D21 -> a Neko VM member is\n32\t  coming) and `overlay_offset` named \"RS20 for Day 20\" (it came true). D19+D20 `d07_analysis_method_count` also says \"for Day 26\n33\t  use the primary classfile named by that unit\" (=> a JVM classfile member on D26, primary class NOT the Main-Class). Grep every\n34\t  new contract for `[A-Z]{2}\\d\\d` tokens, `Day NN` and enum values not seen yet (D21 contract: no new token, no new day number,\n35\t  all 240 carried-over questions byte-identical to D20's).\n36\t- **The theme is asked on its own group only sometimes**: D5-D18 never; D19 (unpacking: `overlay_offset`/`overlay_size`) and D20\n37\t  (resources: + `hcfg_resource_size`) yes; D21 (shared libs) NO -- only per-member `machine` (integer) + config; imports/exports/\n38\t  dlopen handshake unasked = backfill candidates. The D17 backfill re-asked old days' themes on their groups.\n39\t- **Every member since D2 also embeds a \"dynamic trace\" template** (unasked so far): `{\"schema\":\"huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1\",\n40\t  \"branch\":\"<b>\",\"event_count\":<n>,\"campaign\":...,\"family\":\"<lang>_<theme>_trace\",\"effects\":\"...\",\"network\":\"none\"}` gated on env\n41\t  `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (`analysis`/`sandbox`/`workstation`). D18 `fortran_indirect_flow_trace`; D19 `cobol_static_unpack_trace`,\n42\t  effects `memory_only_inert_payload_hash`; D20 `haskell_resource_overlay_trace` / `private_scratch_hash_only`; D21 (in the\n43\t  loader) `ocaml_controlled_dynlink_trace` / `controlled_library_resolution_only`.\n44\t- Question count: 80 on D8, +10/day to 160 on D16, D17 = 204 (backfill #2: every old group padded to 11 ids), then +12/day:\n45\t  D18 216, D19 228, D20 240, **D21 252** (12 new: 2 sha256 + 2 machine + 4 config + 4 plugin_config), no backfill D18-D21. Mastery = `setN.` prefixed copies (2 sets D2-D7, 5 D8-D9, 3 D10-D14,\n46\t  5 D15-D17, 4 D18, 5 D19-D21 = 1260 ids on D21); artifacts named `delivery N: evidence.zip`. Timed end to end: D19 TT 4.2 s /\n47\t  Mastery 10 s; D20 TT 4.8 s / Mastery 9.3 s; D21 TT 4.2 s / Mastery 9.9 s (solve 5.8 s).\n48\t\n49\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n50\t- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, different storage per container (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata,\n51\t  base64 in a constant pool / string literal, raw FPC `.data`, WASM data segment 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D19 packed overlay,\n52\t  D20 RS20 overlay, D21 RAW in the OCaml plugin's `.data` (data symbol `camlPlugin_000__1`; loader: no HCFG at all)):\n53\t  scan raw bytes for `HCFG` and `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*`, decode, accept only if crc32(plain) matches AND the JSON parses -- keep\n54\t  scanning past a failing hit (D9 Nim had two raw decoys); never a fixed offset. Storage did NOT change across a day's variants on\n55\t  any day (D18 offset 8512, D19 overlay 10808/424, D20 overlay 1200888 / resource 380 in single, TT and all 5 Mastery sets\n56\t  while key/campaign/crc re-rolled; D21 plugin/loader machine 62 in every set, campaign BR21-00V re-rolled).\n57\t- **Overlay layout per day (D19 PK19, D20 RS20)** -- both appended exactly at the end of the section-header table\n58\t  (`e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize`), magic `<2 caps><day>`, a fixed header the QUESTION spells field by field:\n59\t  PK19 = `magic | u8 ver | u8 k1 | u8 k2 | pad | u32le packed_len @8 | sha256(unpacked) @12 | packed @44`, unpack\n60\t  `ror8(b ^ k2, 3) ^ k1`, verify sha256, HCFG at out[0]. RS20 = `magic | u8 ver(1) @4 | pad | u32le resource_len @8 | u16le\n61\t  scratch_len @12 | pad | sha256(scratch) @16 | HCFG resource @48 (raw, NOT packed) | scratch` (`private-scratch:<campaign>:inert-only`,\n62\t  35 B); verify `48+res+scratch == len - o` (\"exact end bounds\") and sha256(scratch). Rule: `o = data.rfind(magic)` (\"final\"),\n63\t  read the header widths the question lists, verify bounds + hash, then the normal HCFG xor/crc/JSON at the stated offset;\n64\t  fallback for an unspecified transform = known-plaintext `HCFG` over (xor, rotate, xor). Magic for a field whose question names\n65\t  none (`overlay_size`, `hcfg_resource_size`): the `<2 caps><NN>` token whose digits = the group's day.\n66\t- **Location-as-answer** -- `hcfg_offset` (D9/D11-D14, D17-D18): base-10 FILE offset of the stored blob: base64 -> the `S` of\n67\t  `SENGR...`, RAW -> the `H`. `overlay_offset` (D19): offset of the overlay MAGIC (`P` of PK19); `overlay_size` = file length -\n68\t  that offset (header included: 424 = 44 + 380). D20 `hcfg_resource_size`: the u32le header field at magic+8 (380 = HCFG 12 +\n69\t  368 JSON), NOT the overlay size (463). Record `m.start()` of the validated hit on every scan path.\n70\t- **Storage-as-answer (`hcfg_storage`, D17, enum)** -- rules IN ORDER: `base64` if the crc-valid HCFG appears only after decoding a\n71\t  printable base64 carrier -> `raw_hcfg_section` if literal `HCFG` starts in a section named exactly `.hcfg` -> `wasm_data_segment`\n72\t  -> `raw_const_array` if in any other native data section -> else `raw`. Map offset -> section header; jars = base64. Unknown\n73\t  future token (a packed overlay is in NO section: `raw`? or a new token): read the question's rule list -- the enum is the space.\n74\t- **Any other storage encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data, deadline=None)`** (raw, base64 std/url/wrapped, hex, base32/85,\n75\t  UTF-16, reversed, xor'd, zlib/gzip, multibyte/rolling xor, byte maps, custom/rot13 b64, split/int-array/strided, RC4, AES/TEA/\n76\t  ChaCha, stack-built); `hcfg_find(data)` = first crc-valid + JSON-parsing hit. Kill switch `HCTF_HCFG_SCAN_EXT=0`. It does NOT\n77\t  know the PK19 rotate stub: packer overlays need their own unpack step before the scan.\n78\t- **xor key / config values** -- re-roll per variant (`BRNN-00V`, `node-00V.dayNN...`, crc, key); derive from the header byte.\n79\t- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ `.exe` re-rolls per member in Mastery (d02 C++, d04 Go, d10 Zig PE `pe`). Labels come\n80\t  from THIS member's header. Dispatch on MAGIC, not extension: `7f454c46` ELF, `MZ` PE, `PK` jar, `\\0asm` WASM (next: `NEKO`).\n81\t  A re-asked symbol field on a PE member follows the D2 PE convention: COMDAT section name `.text$<mangled>`. Extensions lie\n82\t  about the role, not the container: D21 `.cmxs` = ELF ET_DYN shared object (OCaml natdynlink plugin).\n83\t- **Member qualifier in the id (multi-member group, D15-D16)** -- `dNN_analysis_<qualifier>_<field>` names ONE member by a token of\n84\t  its FILE NAME. Rule: peel the longest field prefix that is a `[^a-z0-9]+`-separated token of exactly one member name. Tags seen:\n85\t  `stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct` (same HCFG in both), `loader`/`plugin` (D21: roles, HCFG only in the plugin).\n86\t  `sha256_K` = ARCHIVE order (central directory), never sorted.\n87\t- **Member named in the QUESTION, not the id (D21)** -- unqualified `d21_analysis_config_*` say \"Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs\n88\t  member; the loader has no scored HCFG config\"; qualified ones say \"Use the unique d21-- member whose basename ends\n89\t  loader.elf\". Rule: after peeling the id qualifier, if the group still has >1 member, restrict it to the member whose basename\n90\t  ends with the token after `basename ends` / `Use the dNN--` in the question. ORDER MATTERS: run it AFTER the qualifier peel\n91\t  (running it first broke the D15/D16 qualified ids on D21: 26 ids missing from the first POST).\n92\t- **Variant index per group** -- `dNN--variant-XXX` re-rolls per group and mode; a carry-over d01 can re-roll STRIPPED (D15-D17\n93\t  Mastery, D17 TT) -> symbols/disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, `recover_code` `none` (D17 CONFIRMED; the leaf heuristic's\n94\t  8106/8114 rejected); D18 not stripped; D19 TT d01 stripped again (`none` accepted). Pair by sha256, never index.\n95\t- **Contract wording per fetch (D17)** -- the same id's question/answer_format can change between fetches (exact_text -> enum,\n96\t  \"equivalents accepted\"). The solver reads `answer_format` per id at run time; assert enum tokens are in `accepted_values`.\n97\t- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` prefixed ids, each set its own `delivery N: evidence.zip`: pair by sha256. Each set's 1st question\n98\t  ends `Evidence case: dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` (TT `dNN-tt-...`) = set->delivery map.\n99\t- **answer_format.kind for the same field name** -- D8/D15: `elf_class`/`machine` exact_text on d01 but INTEGER (`64`/`62`) on\n100\t  d08/d15 in ONE contract. Dispatch on `kind`, not on the field name.\n101\t- **Feature-presence fields** -- `has_<thing>_section` (D10/D14 literal `.hcfg`), D17 runtime-identity booleans on old groups\n102\t  (`has_go_runtime`, `has_rust_mangled_symbol`, `has_coroutine_runtime`, `has_cpp_typeinfo/vtable`). Generic rule: `has_<x>` = a\n103\t  structural marker of <x> in THIS member; expect `has_overlay`, `has_cobol_runtime`, `has_gnat_*`-style ids next.\n104\t- **Field set per old group** -- old groups gain ids over days (D8 to 10, D17 to 11). Answer by field name from the parsed facts\n105\t  dict of THAT member; unknown field -> log and fall through.\n106\t- **Speed flags (no answer change)** -- per-case timings are usually CPU contention from parallel solver-tests: re-measure with\n107\t  `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py ...`. Floor = AES-CTR+inflate+sha256 of the 67 MB d08 member (~0.35 s/set).\n108\t\n109\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n110\t| You see | First move |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"457eaf39-a8b1-4d3e-9a0d-f840150d9475","uuid":"f5a90523-ed67-4309-9ff0-76ff558cb5c5","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:21:32.918Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md","content":"# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-21; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing