{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nuo4ttgKebu1pyQepobFva","type":"tool_result","content":"[]\n{\"id\": \"contract-forward-hints\", \"concept\": \"The live contract leaks upcoming days: tokens and day numbers that do not belong to today\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19 leaked D20's overlay magic ('PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20') and it came true. Still open after D20: the format enum lists `neko_bytecode` (unseen), and d07_analysis_method_count says 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The solver maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"theme-facts-recording\", \"concept\": \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's (overlay_offset/overlay_size, config after unpacking) and D20's (overlay_offset, hcfg_resource_size) WERE and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256). d20: rs20 version, hcfg_resource_size, scratch_size (35), scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, GHC version 9.12.2.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"new-language-fingerprints\", \"concept\": \"OCaml, V, Odin, Modula-2, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka, Erlang, Julia (Ada D17, Fortran D18, COBOL D19, Haskell D20 seen)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cue strings are in the Recognition cues STEP 3 regex. All still answer format=elf/architecture=x86-64 per the D8-D15 law; risk is only where the HCFG literal lives (compressed Dart snapshot, Nuitka constants blob, GHC closures) -> hcfg_scan then Ghidra. Ada/Fortran/COBOL/Haskell all landed as plain x86-64 ELFs (format elf) -- the law held; D19-D20 moved the HCFG into an overlay instead. gfortran/gnat/ocaml/ghc are NOT installed for fixture builds (apt gfortran gnat ocaml-nox ghc if prebuilds are wanted).\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"ocaml-native-member\", \"concept\": \"OCaml native ELF (ocamlopt): caml symbols, string literals with OCaml block headers, HCFG offset convention\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `caml_startup`, `caml_main`, `camlStdlib__`, `camlDune__exe__Main`, `OCAMLRUNPARAM`. OCaml strings are header-prefixed blocks (word header + padded bytes, last byte = pad count) -> HCFG raw starts at the block payload (offset = the `H`, like D12/D14). Facts: has_ocaml_runtime, module names `camlMain__entry`. ocaml not installed: synthesize a C ELF with OCaml-shaped symbols + a block-wrapped blob.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"native-imports-exports-facts\", \"concept\": \"imports / NEEDED / interpreter / exports lists for ELF, PE, Mach-O\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Generic facts: ELF `needed` (DT_NEEDED order), `imports` (UND .dynsym names, table order, version suffix stripped), `interpreter` (.interp without NUL), `exports` (defined dynsyms); PE import dll list + functions ...\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"shared-object-relocatable\", \"concept\": \"ET_DYN .so / ET_REL .o / DLL members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). gcc -shared and gcc -c fixtures with .hcfg; expected elf_type ET_DYN/ET_REL, entry_point 0x0 for .o, exported-symbol config. PE DLL via objdump -p export ...\"}\n\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_i