symbols, interposed libc names (defined dynsyms whose name is a libc import name: open, getenv, dlsym, __libc_start_main) and whether they call dlsym(RTLD_NEXT). Labels as readelf -V / --dyn-syms prints (`GLIBC_2.2.5`, `@@`). Fixtures: gcc -shared with a version script (-Wl,--version-script) defining V1/V2 of a config getter whose V2 returns the HCFG and V1 a decoy; an LD_PRELOAD shim .so.\"},\n {\"id\":\"library-search-path-facts\",\"concept\":\"How the loader resolves libraries: DT_RPATH vs DT_RUNPATH (incl. $ORIGIN/$LIB tokens), PT_INTERP path, DT_FLAGS_1 (NOW, PIE, NODEFLIB, ORIGIN), SONAME, dlopen path argument absolute/relative\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 trace effects = `controlled_library_resolution_only` -> resolution facts are a likely backfill/next-day field family. lib.binary.elf_loader_facts(data): interpreter, needed (order), soname, rpath, runpath (raw string, not expanded), flags/flags_1 token lists as readelf prints them, has_origin. Plus resolve_library(loader, name, members) that maps a NEEDED/dlopen name to the group member that satisfies it (SONAME match first, then basename). Fixtures: gcc -Wl,-rpath,'$ORIGIN/lib' vs --enable-new-dtags, -Wl,-soname, custom --dynamic-linker.\"},\n {\"id\":\"multi-role-member-router\",\"concept\":\"Groups of 3+ members with roles (loader + several plugins/libraries, stub + payload, client + server), HCFG in one member only, decoy HCFG in another; ids qualified by role or unqualified with the member named in the question text\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21 needed a hand-written _named_member() for unqualified ids whose question says 'Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member; the loader has no scored HCFG config' and it had to run AFTER the qualifier peel. Generalize into lib.binary.route_member(group, field, question) -> (member, residual_field): qualifier peel by longest file-name token, then question phrases ('basename ends X', 'Use the dNN-- X member', 'the member that exports Y', 'the library named by the loader's DT_NEEDED', 'the member loaded by ...'), then structural fallbacks (the only member with a crc-valid HCFG for config_*). Regression: D15/D16/D21 shapes + synthetic 3-member groups (loader, plugin_a, plugin_b) with a decoy HCFG (bad crc) in the loader.\"},\n {\"id\":\"pe-dll-loader-plugin-pair\",\"concept\":\"The D21 shape re-rolled to Windows: loader .exe + plugin .dll (MinGW/MSVC), export directory (names, ordinals, forwarders), import directory, delay-load imports, LoadLibrary/GetProcAddress handshake, DLL side-loading\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"ELF/PE re-rolled per member in Mastery on D2/D4/D10, so a loader/plugin pair may come as PE. lib.binary.pe_link_facts(data): machine (integer and label), characteristics DLL flag, exports [(ordinal, name, rva, forwarder)], import DLLs + functions in directory order, delay imports, TLS callbacks; config in an exported data symbol or .rsrc. Fixtures: x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc if installed, else synthetic PE via lief with an export table and a .hcfg section; check pefile ordinals base.\"},\n {\"id\":\"tls-ifunc-loader-facts\",\"concept\":\"Loader-time code paths: PT_TLS/.tdata/.tbss (TLS initializers holding config), STT_GNU_IFUNC resolvers + IRELATIVE relocs, .init_array/.preinit_array order, DT_INIT/DT_FINI, constructor priorities\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'loader's handshake' read literally. Facts: tls_size/tls_align, tdata bytes (HCFG may sit in .tdata), ifunc symbols + resolver targets (emulate the resolver with unicorn returning a function pointer), init_array entries resolved to symbols in order (RELATIVE addends in PIE!). Extend the built init-time-decoder for ifunc/TLS. Fixtures: gcc __thread char cfg[] = {...}; __attribute__((ifunc)); __attribute__((constructor(101))).\"},\n {\"id\":\"ffi-boundary-exports\",\"concept\":\"Cross-language ABI boundaries: C-ABI exports from Rust cdylib (#[no_mangle]), Go c-shared (cgo `_cgo_`, `crosscall2`, `_cgoexp_`), JNI (`Java_<pkg>_<cls>_<m>`, JNI_OnLoad), Python extension (`PyInit_<mod>`), OCaml C stubs (`caml_*` CAMLprim)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'mind the boundaries' + one-language-per-day: the next pair may be a non-C plugin. lib.binary.ffi_facts(data): ffi kind token (rust_cdylib/go_c_shared/jni/python_ext/ocaml_stub/plain_c), exported C names in dynsym order, demangled JNI class/method from the export name, Go c-shared buildinfo. Fixtures: gcc .so with JNI-shaped exports + PyInit_ export; cargo/go are installed? (check) else synthetic dynsym names.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dwarf-deep-facts\",\"concept\":\"DWARF debug info as answers: CU names and DW_AT_language, DW_AT_producer, comp_dir, subprogram names with low_pc/high_pc, line-table file list, variable/type names (config struct field names)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D21's loader shipped `with debug_info` (OCaml 4.02.3) and D5 Rust had .debug_*; a 'Debug' / 'symbols beyond the symtab' day is plausible. lib.binary.dwarf_facts(data) via pyelftools: cus [(name, language token as llvm-dwarfdump prints e.g. DW_LANG_C11, producer)], functions (JSON), files (JSON line-table order), DWARF version; also .debug_* compressed (SHF_COMPRESSED) handling (built compressed-elf-sections). Fixtures: gcc -g -gdwarf-4/-5, clang-18 -g.\"},\n {\"id\":\"kernel-module-ko-member\",\"concept\":\"Linux kernel module (.ko, ET_REL) as a member: .modinfo key=value strings (license, author, description, vermagic, depends, name), __versions CRCs, init_module/cleanup_module, .gnu.linkonce.this_module\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"User/kernel is the next 'boundary'; .ko is an ELF64 ET_REL (elf_type ET_REL, entry 0x0, machine 62). Facts: modinfo dict in section order, vermagic, depends list, exported symbols (__ksymtab_*), HCFG in .rodata/.data of the relocatable (raw scan works; offset = file offset). Fixture: synthetic ET_REL with a .modinfo section (no kernel headers needed: gcc -c + objcopy --add-section).\"},\n {\"id\":\"macho-dylib-pair\",\"concept\":\"Mach-O loader + dylib pair: LC_LOAD_DYLIB / LC_LOAD_WEAK_DYLIB / LC_RPATH (@rpath, @loader_path, @executable_path), LC_ID_DYLIB, exports trie, chained fixups\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If the pair theme moves to Apple containers (Swift/ObjC were ELF so far; macho label presumed `macho`, prebuilt macho-hcfg-section). lib.binary.macho_link_facts(data) via lief: dylibs in load-command order, rpaths, install name, exported symbols, cputype (integer 16777223 / label x86_64). Fixtures: lief-built Mach-O with a __DATA,__hcfg section and LC_LOAD_DYLIB entries.\"},\n]\nfor x in new: assert x['id'] not in used, x['id']\ng=g+new\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x['priority'])  # stable: keeps relative order inside a priority\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+\"\\n]\\n\"\ns=s[:j]+body+s[k:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(pend),pend)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"\nimport json;s=open('reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md').read();i=s.index('## Readiness gaps');j=s.index('\\`\\`\\`json',i)+8;k=s.index('\\`\\`\\`',j);g=json.loads(s[j:k]);print(len(g), all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g))\"; tail -c 300 reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md; wc -l reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md","description":"Rewrite readiness gaps JSON with new prebuild gaps"}}}
